<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30633" root="عمى" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَامٍ</span></b>  One <i>who does not see his road,</i> or <i>way.</i>
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَامِيَةٌ</span>, applied to a land (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ</span>): see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْمَى</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also, [thus applied,] <i>Of which the
traces are becoming</i> [or <i>become</i>] <i>effaced,</i> or <i>obliterated.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْمَآءٌ</span>, in three places.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  Applied to a woman, (TA,) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَامِيَةٌ</span> signifies
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَكَّآءَةٌ</span>, (K, TA,) [a strange epithet,] meaning
(assumed tropical:)  <i>Having very little milk.</i> (TK.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Applied to
a man, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَامٍ</span> signifies also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَامٍ</span> [i. e. <i>Casting,</i> &amp;c.].
(TA.)

